# This file makes the privacy guarantee travel with the folder. If you copy
# business-os/ into your own repo, these rules come with it — don't delete it.

# Real business data: leads, customer names, invoices, figures. Stays local.
# Leading slash is load-bearing: an unanchored `data/` would also swallow
# templates/data/, which must stay tracked or setup.sh has nothing to copy.
/data/

# API keys.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
